02:48:57,140 --> 02:49:01,980
in accordance with Alabama Code 11-99-4.

2371
02:49:01,980 --> 02:49:03,100
Chair moves for approval.

2372
02:49:03,100 --> 02:49:03,940
Second.

2373
02:49:03,940 --> 02:49:06,620
Second by Mr. Meredith, Mr. Davis.

2374
02:49:06,620 --> 02:49:08,100
Thank you, Madam President.

2375
02:49:08,100 --> 02:49:09,380
Good evening, Council Member Shane Davis,

2376
02:49:09,380 --> 02:49:11,340
Director of Urban Economic Development.

2377
02:49:11,340 --> 02:49:14,380
So there has been, I think, some public confusion

2378
02:49:14,380 --> 02:49:15,620
about this item tonight.

2379
02:49:15,620 --> 02:49:17,900
So you are not approving

2380
02:49:17,900 --> 02:49:20,820
and creating TIF-9 district tonight.

2381
02:49:20,820 --> 02:49:22,300
So per Alabama law,

2382
02:49:22,300 --> 02:49:25,500
there's a series of processes you must go through,

2383
02:49:25,500 --> 02:49:27,460
so does Madison County.

2384
02:49:27,460 --> 02:49:29,460
You did that last council meeting,

2385
02:49:29,460 --> 02:49:30,780
really two council meetings ago,

2386
02:49:30,780 --> 02:49:33,020
you asked the administration, the mayor,

2387
02:49:33,020 --> 02:49:35,460
to bring you a project plan.

2388
02:49:35,460 --> 02:49:37,740
Last meeting, we did that.

2389
02:49:37,740 --> 02:49:41,180
Since that time, we have sent to both Huntsville City Schools,

2390
02:49:41,180 --> 02:49:42,980
Madison County Commission.

2391
02:49:42,980 --> 02:49:45,660
Madison County Commission is the other voting authority

2392
02:49:45,660 --> 02:49:48,660
to create a TIF for Alabama law.

2393
02:49:48,660 --> 02:49:52,460
But you, as the creator of the TIF,

2394
02:49:52,460 --> 02:49:55,660
and would execute the projects within that project plan,

2395
02:49:55,660 --> 02:49:58,780
before you or Madison County votes on it,

2396
02:49:58,780 --> 02:50:01,100
you must certify that the plan hasn't changed

2397
02:50:01,100 --> 02:50:02,980
since it was presented publicly.

2398
02:50:02,980 --> 02:50:06,340
So that would be the boundary of the TIF district

2399
02:50:06,340 --> 02:50:09,980
that was shown hasn't changed since the last presentation

2400
02:50:09,980 --> 02:50:11,780
and the list of projects.

2401
02:50:11,780 --> 02:50:13,780
So tonight, you're simply certifying

2402
02:50:13,780 --> 02:50:16,500
that it is in its final form.

2403
02:50:16,500 --> 02:50:19,620
The next city council meeting, we will publicly go back

2404
02:50:19,620 --> 02:50:22,220
through that, show that to you and the public

2405
02:50:22,220 --> 02:50:23,380
before you vote on it.

2406
02:50:24,900 --> 02:50:26,380
Questions or comments?

2407
02:50:27,540 --> 02:50:28,620
Thank you, Ms. Davis.

2408
02:50:28,620 --> 02:50:30,660
I wanted you to explain that,

2409
02:50:30,660 --> 02:50:32,900
