2414
02:50:40,780 --> 02:50:45,060
We also will talk extensively about this,

2415
02:50:45,060 --> 02:50:47,540
about TIFs at the joint meeting.

2416
02:50:47,540 --> 02:50:48,380
That's right.

2417
02:50:48,380 --> 02:50:49,860
With the school board on Monday,

2418
02:50:49,860 --> 02:50:52,580
if anybody wants to learn more about that.

2419
02:50:52,580 --> 02:50:55,180
There was a question raised, I sent you the email,

2420
02:50:55,180 --> 02:50:57,780
and the question was asked tonight about the funding model.

2421
02:50:57,780 --> 02:51:00,060
Can you just review that, please?

2422
02:51:00,060 --> 02:51:02,580
Yes, so next Thursday, I'll go through that.

2423
02:51:02,580 --> 02:51:05,900
But in preparing any TIF district,

2424
02:51:05,900 --> 02:51:07,900
this will actually be the city's 10th.

2425
02:51:09,060 --> 02:51:12,620
We go through what we call a projection modeling.

2426
02:51:12,620 --> 02:51:14,940
It's not scientifically exact.

2427
02:51:14,940 --> 02:51:16,660
We can't predict the future

2428
02:51:17,780 --> 02:51:20,060
in what private investment will bring.

2429
02:51:20,060 --> 02:51:24,140
But what we do is we have a list of projects,

2430
02:51:24,140 --> 02:51:26,300
then we work with the Mass County Tax Assessor

2431
02:51:26,300 --> 02:51:31,300
to get the base tax proceeds that the district is,

2432
02:51:31,500 --> 02:51:33,460
should it be created, is producing.

2433
02:51:34,380 --> 02:51:37,380
That tax base continues to go to the tax recipients.

2434
02:51:37,380 --> 02:51:39,820
It doesn't go into the TIF district.

2435
02:51:39,820 --> 02:51:42,460
The increment, or the increase that would occur over time

2436
02:51:42,460 --> 02:51:45,860
with new investments would go into the district

2437
02:51:45,860 --> 02:51:48,820
to pay bonds, or if we do a project with cash

2438
02:51:48,820 --> 02:51:50,980
within the tax system, we'd use those tax proceeds

2439
02:51:50,980 --> 02:51:52,340
to just pay cash.

2440
02:51:53,340 --> 02:51:55,420
Kind of a pay as you go model.

2441
02:51:55,420 --> 02:51:59,260
Also, what we do is we project a couple of different things.

2442
02:51:59,260 --> 02:52:01,820
So we know the tax base, we know over time,

2443
02:52:01,820 --> 02:52:06,820
just with inflation and different values increasing over time.

2444
02:52:07,540 --> 02:52:10,300
Say a piece of property five years from now,

2445
02:52:10,300 --> 02:52:12,980
the tax assessor says it's worth 3% more

2446
02:52:12,980 --> 02:52:14,700
than it was when the TIF was created.

2447
02:52:14,700 --> 02:52:18,580
That new increment, increase of that existing tax base

2448
02:52:18,580 --> 02:52:19,940
would go into the district,

2449
02:52:19,940 --> 02:52:22,140
and then you've got new investments.

2450
02:52:22,140 --> 02:52:24,780
So think of Front Row, for instance, and those.

2451
02:52:24,780 --> 02:52:27,180
So we know some of those that are active,

2452
02:52:27,180 --> 02:52:29,020
and we know what that permitted value is,

2453
02:52:29,020 --> 02:52:31,740
so we know what that value will go onto the tax rolls,

2454
02:52:31,740 --> 02:52:34,100
so we can calculate that tax income

2455
02:52:34,100 --> 02:52:35,780
that would come into the district.

2456
02:52:35,780 --> 02:52:38,860
And then we know of areas that are proposed,

2457
02:52:38,860 --> 02:52:40,220
should these improvements make,

2458
02:52:40,220 --> 02:52:42,620
what it would stimulate based on our tax history

2459
02:52:42,620 --> 02:52:45,100
of projects and what they've been produced.

2460
02:52:45,100 --> 02:52:47,580
So we do that, we do some forecasting.

2461
02:52:47,580 --> 02:52:49,580
And we can go into that detail.

2462
02:52:49,580 --> 02:52:52,140
Ms. Smith and I have worked on that for months

2463
02:52:52,140 --> 02:52:57,140
just to try to figure out what we typically do in all TIFs

2464
02:52:57,380 --> 02:52:59,260
is the capital plan will have to,

2465
02:52:59,260 --> 02:53:01,420
what I call seed the TIF.

2466
02:53:01,420 --> 02:53:05,060
So you'll go borrow money and we'll start these projects.

2467
02:53:05,060 --> 02:53:06,700
In the 2014 capital plan,

2468
02:53:06,700 --> 02:53:08,860
we typically two or three years,

2469
02:53:08,860 --> 02:53:12,060
we'll program to fund that early debt service

2470
02:53:12,060 --> 02:53:14,100
to allow that private investment to come online

2471
02:53:14,100 --> 02:53:15,100
and start paying taxes.

2472
02:53:15,100 --> 02:53:16,820
In Alabama, you pay one year in the rear.

2473
02:53:16,820 --> 02:53:18,780
So if you complete something in 2025,

2474
02:53:18,780 --> 02:53:21,540
you don't pay tax till October 26.

2475
02:53:21,540 --> 02:53:23,820
And there, so we have to program all that.

2476
02:53:23,820 --> 02:53:26,700
So we've modeled that, we feel very confident in that model

2477
02:53:26,700 --> 02:53:28,520
in the projects we've presented you.

2478
02:53:28,520 --> 02:53:31,300
That's what you asked the mayor to do about a month ago,

2479
02:53:31,300 --> 02:53:32,700
is present you a plan.

2480
02:53:32,700 --> 02:53:34,800
So we had to go do a lot of that analysis

2481
02:53:34,800 --> 02:53:37,780
to come up with something we could present to you

2482
02:53:37,780 --> 02:53:39,740
that we were confident that the district

2483
02:53:39,740 --> 02:53:41,100
would be able to afford.

2484
02:53:41,100 --> 02:53:43,740
And it is your belief that the incremental growth

2485
02:53:43,740 --> 02:53:45,660
that's going to result in this district

2486
02:53:45,660 --> 02:53:48,380
will be sufficient to pay back the debt

2487
02:53:48,380 --> 02:53:50,580
on the VBC and the other projects.

2488
02:53:50,580 --> 02:53:54,180
We do, actually our model shows it would pay off early.

2489
02:53:54,180 --> 02:53:55,020
Pay off early.

2490
02:53:55,020 --> 02:53:57,180
And early would be in the next.

2491
02:53:57,180 --> 02:53:58,580
You know, it's not a crystal ball,

2492
02:53:58,580 --> 02:53:59,940
but we're very conservative.

2493
02:53:59,940 --> 02:54:03,540
So, you know, we don't wanna say 10 years and it go 15.

2494
02:54:03,540 --> 02:54:05,300
Right now our conservative model

2495
02:54:05,300 --> 02:54:07,160
is somewhere 15 or 16 years.

2496
02:54:07,160 --> 02:54:09,180
Under the statute, it can go as long as 30.

2497
02:54:09,180 --> 02:54:10,820
So half time.

2498
02:54:10,820 --> 02:54:12,300
And you have been very successful

2499
02:54:12,300 --> 02:54:14,620
with your modeling on past TIFs.

2500
02:54:14,620 --> 02:54:16,140
We're very conservative on it, yes.

2501
02:54:16,140 --> 02:54:16,980
Thank you.

2502
02:54:16,980 --> 02:54:18,100
We don't wanna give bad news.

2503
02:54:18,100 --> 02:54:19,140
Question for Mr. Mayor.

2504
02:54:19,140 --> 02:54:21,100
Going back a little bit,

2505
02:54:21,100 --> 02:54:23,020
you said the next time we would be

2506
02:54:24,820 --> 02:54:28,780
dealing with the TIF would be on the 11th.

2507
02:54:28,780 --> 02:54:29,600
Yes, sir.

2508
02:54:29,600 --> 02:54:32,520
I presume that means that the county

2509
02:54:32,520 --> 02:54:35,120
will have already voted on the issue.

2510
02:54:35,120 --> 02:54:37,580
Yes, so in all TIFs, whether they're in

2511
02:54:37,580 --> 02:54:39,860
Limestone County, we've done two.

2512
02:54:39,860 --> 02:54:42,780
This will be our eighth in Madison County since 2000.

2513
02:54:42,780 --> 02:54:45,340
So almost 26 years.

2514
02:54:45,340 --> 02:54:48,320
In doing TIF districts here, they've all been successful.

2515
02:54:48,320 --> 02:54:51,540
We always let the county vote first

2516
02:54:51,540 --> 02:54:54,700
because you can't vote and then commit yourself

2517
02:54:54,700 --> 02:54:57,720
or our taxpayers to the debt service of the projects

2518
02:54:57,720 --> 02:55:00,220
without both bodies voting affirmative.

2519
02:55:00,220 --> 02:55:01,780
So we let the county vote first,

2520
02:55:01,780 --> 02:55:03,460
whether it's in Madison County, Limestone County,

2521
02:55:03,460 --> 02:55:05,260
and then the very next meeting,

2522
02:55:05,260 --> 02:55:06,580
this body would take it up.

2523
02:55:06,580 --> 02:55:10,740
And that would be the last that we have to vote on this.

2524
02:55:10,740 --> 02:55:12,220
Yes, sir, you're correct.

2525
02:55:12,220 --> 02:55:14,860
Once you did that, we would make file to the tax assessor

2526
02:55:14,860 --> 02:55:17,460
that both bodies have approved the TIF district

2527
02:55:17,460 --> 02:55:20,300
has been created and then we would set forth

2528
02:55:20,300 --> 02:55:21,700
executing the plan.

2529
02:55:21,700 --> 02:55:25,500
And the clock starts, I believe, the following Monday?

2530
02:55:25,500 --> 02:55:26,980
It would, yes, sir.

2531
02:55:26,980 --> 02:55:27,800
Thank you, sir.

2532
02:55:27,800 --> 02:55:30,300
And we believe that the June 3rd

2533
02:55:30,300 --> 02:55:32,020
commission meeting is when the...

2534
02:55:32,020 --> 02:55:34,620
Intentively, our TIF calendar would request

2535
02:55:34,620 --> 02:55:37,220
that Madison County Commission take it up then.

2536
02:55:37,220 --> 02:55:39,220
Certainly, if they decided to postpone,

2537
02:55:39,220 --> 02:55:41,780
we would shift everybody to the very next meeting.

2538
02:55:41,780 --> 02:55:43,940
And we have until the end of June to do that

2539
02:55:43,940 --> 02:55:45,460
based on our timeline.

2540
02:55:45,460 --> 02:55:46,300
That's right, yes, ma'am.

2541
02:55:46,300 --> 02:55:47,140
Thank you.

2542
02:55:47,140 --> 02:55:48,060
Mr. Kling, did you have a question?

2543
02:55:48,060 --> 02:55:51,560
Well, just to be redundant, but just to double check,

2544
02:55:51,560 --> 02:55:54,080
every other TIF that we've had in the past,

2545
02:55:54,080 --> 02:55:57,180
they've all been paid off and paid off a little bit early,

2546
02:55:57,180 --> 02:55:58,180
